## Large binaries - see AGENTS.md, "Large tracked files"
# Two large files are tracked on purpose and are named there. Decision D4 is
# that they are DOCUMENTED, not rewritten: no filter-repo, no BFG, no git-lfs,
# so anything big committed here is permanent for everyone who ever clones the
# repo. These rules exist so nothing of the same shape joins them by accident.
# Both exceptions are negations rather than a narrower pattern, so the rule
# still bites if either file is ever moved or renamed.
*.onnx
!resources/models/yolov10m.onnx
*.gif
!images/Rust.gif
# other model-weight formats - none tracked, none wanted
*.pt
*.pth
*.safetensors
*.tflite
*.gguf
# video
*.mp4
*.mkv
*.mov
*.webm
# build/packaging output and signing material (dist/ is ignored already, but
# these get copied around by hand)
*.msix
*.msixbundle
*.appx
*.appxbundle
*.msi
*.pfx
*.cer
*.zip
*.7z
*.tgz
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tar.zst
# NOT ignored on purpose: *.bin (glTF buffers), *.gltf, *.glb, *.ktx2, *.png -
# the renderer's test assets are exactly those and they are small.

